 from Hebrew literature and Israeli culture through the use of texts and audiovisual materials.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(CA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: HEBRW 1103\u00a0or above or permission of instructor.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2727, "crseId": 353534, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "HEBRW", "catalogNbr": "3105", "titleShort": "Life in Israel", "titleLong": "Life in Israel: Aspects of Israeli Society, Language and Literature", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 16658, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:30PM", "timeEnd": "04:25PM", "startDt": "01/22/2019", "endDt": "05/07/2019", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "ns21", "firstName": "Nava", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Scharf"}], "pattern": "W", "facilityDescr": "White Hall 114", "bldgDescr": "White Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "WHT114", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/22/2019", "endDt": "05/07/2019", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "JWST", "catalogNbr": "3105", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/22/2019", "sessionEndDt": "05/07/2019", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "In this advanced Hebrew course we will be reading selected and relevant articles dealing with life in Israel. Students will focus on language skills and interests while paying attention to vocabulary building, grammar review, and literary analysis of modern texts.\u00a0 We also will be reading stories, poetry; view and discuss Israeli TV programs and news broadcasts. Authors may include: N. Gutman, D. Shahar, O. Kastel-Bloom, E. Keret, and A. Oz.\u00a0 Poets may include: Y. Amichai, D. Avidan, D. Pagis, D. Rabikovitz, N. Zack. \u00a0\u00a0In addition, we will be reading a few modern children stories and will have a discussion of present-day influences on Israeli children's literature.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(LA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: HEBRW 3102,\u00a0HEBRW 3104, HEBRW 3108\u00a0or permission of instructor.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2727, "crseId": 353554, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "HEBRW", "catalogNbr": "4102", "titleShort": "Biblical Hebrew Prose: Genesis", "titleLong": "Biblical Hebrew Prose: Genesis", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 16669, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "12:20PM", "timeEnd": "02:15PM", "startDt": "01/22/2019", "endDt": "05/07/2019", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "lm283", "firstName": "Lauren", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Monroe"}], "pattern": "W", "facilityDescr": "Lincoln Hall 117", "bldgDescr": "Lincoln Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "LNC117", "meetingTopicDescription": null}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/22/2019", "endDt": "05/07/2019", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "Biblical Hebrew Prose: Genesis", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "HEBRW", "catalogNbr": "6102", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "JWST", "catalogNbr": "4102", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "RELST", "catalogNbr": "4102", "type": "B"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/22/2019", "sessionEndDt": "05/07/2019", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "From the Garden of Eden to Noah's Ark, from Abraham's journey from Haran to Joseph's coat of many colors, the book of Genesis contains stories that are at once familiar to Western readers, and foreign in their ancient Near Eastern setting.\u00a0 Through reading the book of Genesis in the original Hebrew, this course will address issues such as how the Israelites understood their origins, and their relationships with their God, Yahweh, their neighbors, and the land of Canaan itself, as well as how these themes are developed in biblical myth and folklore. Close attention will be paid to matters of grammar, syntax, and vocabulary in order to develop students' skills in reading biblical Hebrew prose and to enhance their understanding of the Hebrew language itself as a window on ancient Israelite thought. Students will be expected to utilize commentaries, biblical Hebrew grammars and lexicons in their preparation of assigned texts.", "catalogBreadth": "(GHB)", "catalogDistr": "(LA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "Co-meets with HEBRW 6102.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: prior training in Biblical Hebrew or permission of instructor.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2727, "crseId": 367498, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "HEBRW", "catalogNbr": "6102", "titleShort": "Biblical Hebrew Prose: Genesis", "titleLong": "Biblical Hebrew Prose: Genesis", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 16672, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "12:20PM", "timeEnd": "02:15PM", "startDt": "01/22/2019", "endDt": "05/07/2019", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "lm283", "firstName": "Lauren", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Monroe"}], "pattern": "W", "facilityDescr": "Lincoln Hall 117", "bldgDescr": "Lincoln Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "LNC117", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/22/2019", "endDt": "05/07/2019", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "HEBRW", "catalogNbr": "4102", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "JWST", "catalogNbr": "4102", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "RELST", "catalogNbr": "4102", "type": "B"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/22/2019", "sessionEndDt": "05/07/2019", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "The books of 1 and 2 Samuel tell the riveting story of the rise to power of Israel's kings Saul and David.\u00a0 In this class we will read these books in the original Hebrew, paying attention to details of character and plot development, as well as issues of compositional history and the relationship of biblical narrative to ancient Israelite history.\u00a0 Students' weekly preparation will involve translation with close attention to lexical, grammatical and syntactic issues raised by the Hebrew texts, as well as work with commentaries and other secondary literature.\u00a0 Students grades will be based on class participation and preparation, an in-class presentation and a final research paper.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "Co-meets with HEBRW 4102/JWST 4102.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: prior training in Biblical Hebrew or permission of instructor required.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}]}, "message": null, "meta": {"copyright": "Cornell University, Office of the University Registrar", "rosterDttm": "2019-06-02T19:14:21-0400", "catalogDttm": "2019-06-02T19:15:24-0400"}}